WEBVTT

00:00:01.114 --> 00:00:12.992
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.126 --> 00:00:18.699
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:25.628
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.139 --> 00:00:37.175
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.351 --> 00:00:43.290
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:50.696
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:58.505
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:05.379
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:10.984
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:17.257
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:25.687
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:33.707 --> 00:01:36.710
Over and over it has
been recorded.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:38.945
Look! From these descriptions alone,

00:01:38.945 --> 00:01:41.379
you can see they've appeared
13 times in 500 years.

00:01:41.548 --> 00:01:44.718
Dying... Reawakening...

00:01:44.718 --> 00:01:47.053
Children who live on and on.

00:01:47.053 --> 00:01:49.122
What is their purpose?!

00:01:49.122 --> 00:01:52.492
Horrifying demons!
Vampires of death!

00:01:52.492 --> 00:01:55.395
Never resting undead!

00:01:55.395 --> 00:01:57.264
The Children of Befort.

00:01:57.264 --> 00:02:01.067
They deliberately appear again and
again, meddling with humanity.

00:02:01.067 --> 00:02:04.671
The code in that fragment...
A book of revelations?

00:02:04.671 --> 00:02:07.140
They don't die.
(Or the words of the devil?)

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:10.310
They just pretend to die, and decades
later, they rise from their graves.

00:02:10.310 --> 00:02:11.945
And creep into homes with children!

00:02:11.945 --> 00:02:15.882
They kill the children and
pretend to be part of the family!

00:02:15.882 --> 00:02:18.146
And then they appear again!

00:02:18.251 --> 00:02:21.618
(50 years later.) I must hurry! (100
years later.) No one knows of this yet!

00:02:21.655 --> 00:02:23.523
(They cry out at their evil rebirth!)
Of course, the graves!

00:02:23.523 --> 00:02:23.924
I have to unearth the graves and
kill them while they sleep!

00:02:23.924 --> 00:02:25.826
I have to unearth the graves and
kill them while they sleep!
FROM THE EDGE OF NIGHT

00:02:25.826 --> 00:02:25.859
FROM THE EDGE OF NIGHT

00:02:25.859 --> 00:02:27.961
I'll dig them up from their
graves and burn them!
FROM THE EDGE OF NIGHT

00:02:27.961 --> 00:02:28.795
Monsters! Monsters!
FROM THE EDGE OF NIGHT

00:02:28.795 --> 00:02:30.820
Monsters! Monsters!

00:04:19.072 --> 00:04:22.375
-Conrad?! Conrad!
-Mother!!

00:04:22.375 --> 00:04:26.277
What's the matter, Conrad?
You had a scary dream, didn't you?

00:04:26.513 --> 00:04:29.482
It's alright now. Come on.

00:04:31.518 --> 00:04:36.421
1853 HOLLAND

00:04:54.741 --> 00:04:58.006
-Big brother?
-What is it, Conrad?

00:05:25.071 --> 00:05:28.041
But mom is always scolding us!

00:05:28.041 --> 00:05:31.033
You shouldn't say things like that, Claud.

00:05:31.211 --> 00:05:33.907
It only shows how much she cares about...

00:05:35.749 --> 00:05:37.740
What's the matter?

00:05:43.757 --> 00:05:46.426
Claud... Go home ahead of me.

00:05:46.426 --> 00:05:48.826
-But...
-Just do it!

00:05:49.062 --> 00:05:50.427
Okay.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:08.771
Palza...

00:06:12.585 --> 00:06:15.789
We searched everywhere
for you, Palza.

00:06:15.789 --> 00:06:19.693
Didn't you receive the postcard?
Why didn't you come?

00:06:19.693 --> 00:06:23.129
We were worried something
might have gone wrong.

00:06:23.863 --> 00:06:25.854
Now, let's go...

00:06:27.167 --> 00:06:30.500
Don't tell me you're actually
thinking of staying here?

00:06:31.404 --> 00:06:33.998
And what if I am thinking of staying?!

00:06:34.641 --> 00:06:36.734
I can't take this anymore!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.470
I'm going to stay here!

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:43.440
What's brought this on
all of a sudden, Palza?

00:06:43.516 --> 00:06:46.119
Sudden? You call this sudden!?

00:06:46.119 --> 00:06:49.189
This isn't sudden!
You all know what I mean!

00:06:49.189 --> 00:06:52.386
What we did was wrong!

00:06:52.592 --> 00:06:57.063
I'm tired of it. I want to stay here.

00:06:57.063 --> 00:06:59.766
I am Conrad Rugen.

00:06:59.766 --> 00:07:02.368
Coward! Traitor!

00:07:02.368 --> 00:07:05.565
What's going to happen to me
with you gone?!

00:07:05.805 --> 00:07:07.807
Please, Palza!

00:07:07.807 --> 00:07:10.977
Palza, no matter what your feelings...

00:07:10.977 --> 00:07:13.613
we can't just accept that.

00:07:13.613 --> 00:07:16.104
-Stand up, Palza!
-Conrad!

00:07:16.216 --> 00:07:18.241
Conrad!

00:07:18.685 --> 00:07:20.787
-Conrad!
-Mother!

00:07:20.787 --> 00:07:22.856
-Conrad!
-Mother!

00:07:22.856 --> 00:07:25.188
Mother!

00:07:49.182 --> 00:07:51.514
Goodbye, Conrad...

00:07:51.918 --> 00:07:54.478
Conrad Rugen.

00:08:02.295 --> 00:08:07.100
The new type of radiation discovered
by Professor Conrad Rugen.

00:08:07.100 --> 00:08:09.302
Just as light can pass
through glass...

00:08:09.302 --> 00:08:09.669
Just as light can pass
through glass...
1901 SEEDEN

00:08:09.669 --> 00:08:09.702
1901 SEEDEN

00:08:09.702 --> 00:08:13.373
these rays pass through solids
like wood and human flesh.
1901 SEEDEN

00:08:13.373 --> 00:08:14.107
1901 SEEDEN

00:08:14.107 --> 00:08:14.674
With this sensational discovery...
1901 SEEDEN

00:08:14.674 --> 00:08:16.643
With this sensational discovery...

00:08:16.643 --> 00:08:23.310
physicists around the world will be
exploring its possibilities for years.

00:08:24.083 --> 00:08:27.320
This is a great contribution
to mankind...

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.523
that will surely result in
the conferment of a Nobel Prize.

00:08:30.523 --> 00:08:35.620
A reflection of all the effort
put into it by the creator.

00:08:48.007 --> 00:08:50.805
-Hesma!
-It's confirmed.

00:08:50.944 --> 00:08:52.935
Let's go.

00:09:01.821 --> 00:09:05.780
SOUTH EASTERN ARCHIPELAGO

00:09:08.695 --> 00:09:11.960
CLAIRMONT SANATORIUM & HOSPITAL

00:09:30.016 --> 00:09:32.041
Where is she?!

00:09:33.686 --> 00:09:36.712
Excuse me...
Who are you?

00:09:37.924 --> 00:09:39.959
Tina!

00:09:39.959 --> 00:09:42.291
She just passed away...

00:09:42.862 --> 00:09:47.196
However, I think you children have
mistaken her for someone else.

00:09:53.106 --> 00:09:55.199
We're too late!

00:09:55.308 --> 00:09:59.244
She was called "Serafine."
That was her name.

00:09:59.779 --> 00:10:02.577
Serafine...

00:10:29.342 --> 00:10:32.641
What was... What was her age?

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:37.283
Forty two... I believe.

00:10:37.283 --> 00:10:39.649
Forty two years ago...

00:10:40.186 --> 00:10:42.722
She was born in 1859.

00:10:42.722 --> 00:10:46.818
Yes. I think that's right. What of it?

00:10:52.231 --> 00:10:56.536
I wouldn't mind, could you
stay by her side for a little while?

00:10:56.536 --> 00:10:59.339
She has been alone
most of her life.

00:10:59.339 --> 00:11:02.408
She doesn't have any particular friends.

00:11:02.408 --> 00:11:06.401
I have to inform the director
of her passing.

00:11:13.453 --> 00:11:15.922
1859.

00:11:15.922 --> 00:11:19.688
Exactly 100 years after
Christina's death.

00:11:20.159 --> 00:11:22.423
What's wrong, Mel?

00:11:24.263 --> 00:11:26.254
Mel!

00:11:29.469 --> 00:11:31.664
I...

00:11:35.008 --> 00:11:38.205
It's alright.
Get a hold of yourself.

00:11:42.582 --> 00:11:45.380
Who... are you?

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.011
Mel?!

00:12:00.299 --> 00:12:02.301
Dumas!

00:12:02.301 --> 00:12:04.826
So, you're all here.

00:12:06.672 --> 00:12:09.140
Let me give you all a piece of advice...

00:12:09.509 --> 00:12:12.637
It's about time you started
cooperating with me.

00:12:12.979 --> 00:12:14.970
It's no use, Dumas.

00:12:15.348 --> 00:12:17.908
We can't help you.

00:12:18.451 --> 00:12:20.442
And we don't want to.

00:12:21.988 --> 00:12:26.322
You can't keep saying that forever.
You monsters!

00:12:27.126 --> 00:12:29.253
You're all just monsters!

00:12:29.295 --> 00:12:32.856
Someday you'll all get stakes
through your hearts.

00:12:46.779 --> 00:12:48.838
Now!

00:12:52.018 --> 00:12:54.111
Mel! Hurry!

00:12:54.954 --> 00:12:56.945
Mel!

00:13:02.061 --> 00:13:04.154
Mel!

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:10.336
-Mel...
-It's too late, Hasmodye!

00:13:10.336 --> 00:13:12.531
She's no longer Mel!

00:13:13.506 --> 00:13:15.531
Forget them!

00:13:28.955 --> 00:13:31.856
One of them is enough.

00:13:35.261 --> 00:13:37.286
I see...

00:13:37.563 --> 00:13:40.032
This is where you were.

00:13:40.032 --> 00:13:42.023
And now...

00:13:42.335 --> 00:13:45.236
You're gone.

00:13:51.611 --> 00:13:57.345
111 YEARS LATER

00:14:16.135 --> 00:14:19.935
2012 SOUTH EASTERN ARCHIPELAGO

00:14:41.694 --> 00:14:44.492
What's wrong?
Is that all you've got, Thoma?

00:14:46.165 --> 00:14:48.901
Even though this is practice,
if you lose your concentration...

00:14:48.901 --> 00:14:51.233
It's as good as asking for death.

00:14:55.608 --> 00:14:57.610
Thoma!

00:14:57.610 --> 00:15:00.580
Hey! Thoma!
Your practice isn't over yet!

00:15:00.580 --> 00:15:04.038
It's time, it's time! It's time
for me to go pick up Mom!

00:15:04.383 --> 00:15:06.374
Unbelievable!

00:15:17.997 --> 00:15:20.056
Yahoo!

00:15:36.983 --> 00:15:38.974
A boat.

00:15:42.221 --> 00:15:44.246
Chikao?

00:16:15.388 --> 00:16:17.857
What are you doing in a place like this?

00:16:17.857 --> 00:16:20.426
There's a boat on the shore
with the name "Chikao" on it.

00:16:20.426 --> 00:16:22.519
Is that where you came from?

00:16:26.032 --> 00:16:29.934
Hey! I know you can hear me.
You could at least answer!

00:16:33.205 --> 00:16:35.775
What the? Fine, whatever.

00:16:35.775 --> 00:16:38.344
There are poisonous snakes
and bees around here.

00:16:38.344 --> 00:16:40.574
If you get bit it'll kill you!

00:16:47.053 --> 00:16:49.283
You better go home before it gets dark!

00:16:56.796 --> 00:16:59.264
What's with her?!

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:25.113
[Chanting]

00:17:31.664 --> 00:17:33.666
I see it!

00:17:33.666 --> 00:17:36.702
I see a flower for the young couple.

00:17:36.702 --> 00:17:40.673
Flowers are good!
Young and beautiful lady.

00:17:40.673 --> 00:17:44.877
You are carrying a flower
hidden beneath your clothing.

00:17:44.877 --> 00:17:47.471
You're going to be very happy!

00:17:47.613 --> 00:17:49.849
Yes, thank you!

00:17:49.849 --> 00:17:54.149
Take good care of your flower! If you
come to the island again please stop by!

00:17:54.754 --> 00:17:58.520
-Thoma, when did you get here?
-You really go all out.

00:17:59.158 --> 00:18:02.150
The right atmosphere is very
important in fortunetelling.

00:18:02.395 --> 00:18:06.161
But you're never going to show
that dance to Dad, are you?

00:18:06.332 --> 00:18:10.436
Don't tease me, Thoma. It's thanks
to this that we're able to eat!

00:18:10.436 --> 00:18:12.666
-Yeah, yeah!
-Hey, hold it!

00:18:18.411 --> 00:18:20.513
Damn it!

00:18:20.513 --> 00:18:22.572
My goodness.

00:18:23.516 --> 00:18:25.518
Thoma?

00:18:25.518 --> 00:18:27.986
There's no where to run!

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:32.518
Stupid kid! You've been
nothing but trouble!

00:18:33.926 --> 00:18:36.520
Just stay where you are.

00:18:44.303 --> 00:18:47.306
-We did it!
-Let me go!

00:18:47.306 --> 00:18:51.644
You were being chased by bad guys,
right? I am a champion of justice!

00:18:51.644 --> 00:18:53.746
Are you stupid?!

00:18:53.746 --> 00:18:57.049
-Go around the other side!
-Don't sweat it! This way!

00:18:57.049 --> 00:19:00.453
-What are you doing?!
-Shut up! Let go of my hand!

00:19:00.453 --> 00:19:03.013
Stop being a pain, Chitto!

00:19:03.456 --> 00:19:05.491
Hey! Woah!

00:19:05.491 --> 00:19:08.153
You can't run any more! Chitto!

00:19:08.761 --> 00:19:10.796
Hey! Your name's Chitto?

00:19:10.796 --> 00:19:12.998
Go away! Don't follow me!

00:19:12.998 --> 00:19:16.331
Geez! You're in my way!
Stupid moron!

00:19:16.502 --> 00:19:19.939
Ha ha! Very funny!
You stole something, didn't you?

00:19:19.939 --> 00:19:23.142
- You moron!
- You've got a bad mouth!

00:19:23.142 --> 00:19:25.744
-I'm not gonna help you.
No one asked you to!

00:19:25.744 --> 00:19:28.076
Mind your own business!

00:19:28.247 --> 00:19:30.238
Little brat!

00:19:30.816 --> 00:19:32.909
Guess there's no choice!

00:19:40.793 --> 00:19:42.920
-Huh?
-What was that?

00:19:44.463 --> 00:19:46.488
Ow, ow!

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:49.528
Uh oh...

00:19:52.104 --> 00:19:54.129
Chitto...

00:19:56.175 --> 00:19:58.166
H-Hey...!

00:20:00.079 --> 00:20:03.182
-Where is Helga?
-I don't know. Nothing to do with me.

00:20:03.182 --> 00:20:07.619
One of the kids saw both of you
run off together!

00:20:07.786 --> 00:20:11.779
So, you're the decoy?
Never mind. We're going back.

00:20:15.528 --> 00:20:17.519
See ya!

00:20:19.665 --> 00:20:21.895
What's with him?

00:20:23.135 --> 00:20:25.204
So he was from Chikao.

00:20:25.204 --> 00:20:27.806
That place has a bad reputation.

00:20:27.806 --> 00:20:31.469
I heard that a child ran away
from there recently.

00:20:32.978 --> 00:20:34.969
Chikao?

00:20:39.184 --> 00:20:41.787
Thoma, it's almost
dinner time!

00:20:41.787 --> 00:20:44.779
-Come right back!
-Okay!

00:21:14.253 --> 00:21:16.956
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:21:16.956 --> 00:21:20.858
I'm just glad nothing happened
to the little girl, director.

00:21:21.026 --> 00:21:23.017
Well then...

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:43.382
Who's that girl?!

00:21:43.382 --> 00:21:45.718
They said she ran away
from the orphanage.

00:21:45.718 --> 00:21:48.454
Your father found her all alone
on the south shore

00:21:48.454 --> 00:21:50.251
and contacted them right away.

00:21:50.289 --> 00:21:52.291
Did you ask her why she did it? Why?!

00:21:52.291 --> 00:21:54.326
I'm sure she has a reason.

00:21:54.326 --> 00:21:57.784
But we had to contact them
no matter what, Thoma.

00:22:35.634 --> 00:22:45.441
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:45.711 --> 00:22:55.554
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:55.554 --> 00:23:00.287
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:00.325 --> 00:23:05.160
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:05.564 --> 00:23:14.700
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:14.840 --> 00:23:19.878
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:19.878 --> 00:23:25.150
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:25.150 --> 00:23:29.553
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:29.588 --> 00:23:33.892
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:33.892 --> 00:23:38.761
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
